course: dictionary
lesson: 13337
title: Spinning that keeps steady
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gyroscopic means to do with a gyroscope, or behaving like one. A gyroscope is a spinning wheel or disc. Once it spins fast, it resists being tipped over and stays steady.
explain: «The spinning top stayed upright on the table.» The clues are spinning and upright. The spin is what keeps the top steady, so a top that stays up because it spins is showing a gyroscopic effect.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. «The gyroscopic wheel stayed steady» still makes sense, so gyroscopic is about steadiness that comes from spinning.
fact: A gyroscope is a spinning wheel or disc that keeps steady and resists being tipped over.
fact: Gyroscopic means to do with a gyroscope, or behaving like one.
fact: Gyroscopic effects help explain why a spinning top stays up and why a moving bicycle is easier to balance.
fact: Phones, drones and planes use gyroscopic sensors to know which way they are tilted.
fact: Spinning also helps a frisbee fly straight, because of gyroscopic stability.
exercise: «A phone uses a gyroscopic sensor to know how it is tilted.» What does gyroscopic mean here? | Loud and ringing | To do with a battery charger | Soft and bendy | *To do with a spinning wheel that keeps steady
exercise: «A moving bicycle is easier to balance because of gyroscopic effects.» What helps the bike stay steady? | Its bell | *Spinning wheels that resist being tipped over | A soft seat | Its colour
exercise: Which word means steady because it spins? | bright | slow | *gyroscopic | loud
test: «The gyroscopic sensor told the drone which way it was tilted.» What job does the sensor do? | Plays music | *Tells the drone which way it is tilted | Makes the drone faster | Paints the drone
test: Which of these is a gyroscope? | A wooden box | *A spinning disc that resists being tipped over | A pencil case | A frisbee cup
exam: Why does a spinning top stay upright? | *Because its spin makes it steady and resistant to tipping | Because it is painted bright colours | Because it is heavy and sits on a flat table | Because someone holds it still
